<title>DENMARK: FLS Aerospace signs UK maintenance deals.</title>
<headline>FLS Aerospace signs UK maintenance deals.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish engineering group FLS Industries said on Thursday its UK-based FLS Aerospace unit signed major maintenance contracts with leading British air charter operators Airworld and Leisure International.</p>
<p>It said the contracts, worth 150 million crowns in all, embraced all-round maintenance including technical service and components and equipment supply over an unspecified number of years for Airbus A321 aircraft on order for the two operators.</p>
<p>FLS Aerospace said it already had a large stock of Airbus A320 components, which could be used on the new planes.</p>
<p>It said the new deal was a continuation of previous cooperation with Airworld and Leisure International on aircraft maintenance services.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
